  "conclusion": "The 16^3 cache shows a repeatable GPU-render reduction only at the screen-filling scale (-0.104, -0.312 and -0.032 ms paired across all three runs; median paired delta -0.104 ms). Whole-frame deltas remain effectively flat (-0.002, +0.125, -0.008 ms), while CPU cache encoding increases (+0.018, +0.048, +0.001 ms). All other cache/scale combinations have small mixed GPU changes and no consistent whole-frame gain. Keep direct sampling as default and cache disabled unless a game explicitly opts in; do not claim a total-frame win. At every fixed scale, 16^3 is closer to direct than 8^3 in the captured image while using 32 KiB versus 4 KiB."
